    "summary_one_sentence": "A gifted high school runner takes an unskilled classmate under his wing, unknowingly fostering a fierce track-and-field rival who will challenge him for years to come.",
    "summary_short": "When a talented young runner agrees to mentor a determined but uncoordinated classmate, he expects to share his passion for track and field. However, through relentless discipline and raw dedication, the novice rapidly closes the skill gap between them. What begins as a simple mentorship soon evolves into an intense, long-term athletic rivalry that transforms both of their lives. Ultimately, both athletes must push past their personal limits to define what victory truly means to them on and off the track.",
    "summary_long": "In the competitive world of high school athletics, a exceptionally gifted runner stands at the top of his discipline, seemingly unmatched in speed and dedication. Driven by a desire to share his love for the sport, he takes a struggling, uncoordinated classmate under his wing to teach him the fundamentals of track and field. The newcomer possesses little initial skill, but his unwavering willpower and obsession with improvement drive him to train harder than anyone anticipated. Day after day, the duo logs endless laps together, building an unexpected bond rooted in shared sweat and exhaustion. As the seasons pass, the once-unskilled student undergoes a dramatic transformation, rapidly shaving seconds off his time and closing in on his mentor's records. Realizing that his former pupil is fast becoming a formidable contender, the veteran runner is forced to confront his own plateau and fear of losing his dominance. Their relationship shifts from friendly guidance to a tense, electric rivalry that captivates their peers and coaches alike. Every race becomes a psychological and physical battleground where neither athlete is willing to concede an inch. Over the course of several years, their relentless pursuit of excellence challenges both runners to push beyond their perceived physical boundaries and reevaluate their individual motives for running.",
